<title>USA: Abbey Nat'l to price $500 mln in debt in US.</title>
<headline>Abbey Nat'l to price $500 mln in debt in US.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Abbey National Plc is expected to price $500 million in perpetual bonds on Wednesday, said lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal will be priced today and has been upped in size to $500 million,&quot; said a Salomon syndicate source.</p>
<p>Market talk on the deal earlier called for $300 million of a noncall 10-year perpetual bond, however, later was upped in size to meet investor demand, the underwriter said.</p>
<p>Price talk on the issue is seen between 77 to 79 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, syndicate sources said.</p>
<p>--Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675</p>
</text>
